{"name":"Toothpick","hex":"#bf843b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"toothpick","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small, usually wooden, stick, often pointed at both ends, for removing food residue from between the teeth.","A very thin individual."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To spear food on a toothpick.","To transfer a sample of bacteria, etc. by means of a toothpick."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toothpick"}],"entries":[{"title":"Toothpick","blocks":[{"text":"A toothpick is a small thin stick of wood, plastic, bamboo, metal, bone or other substance with at least one and sometimes two pointed ends to insert between teeth to remove detritus, usually after a meal. Toothpicks are also used in food decoration and tableware as cocktail skewers; they are used to hold or spear small appetizers, and can be decorated with plastic frills, small paper umbrellas or flags."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Holzzahnstocher.jpg/330px-Holzzahnstocher.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toothpick","wikidata":"Q41331"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Oral_B_toothpicks_dental_woodsticks.jpg/500px-Oral_B_toothpicks_dental_woodsticks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Oral_B_toothpicks_dental_woodsticks.jpg/1280px-Oral_B_toothpicks_dental_woodsticks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Oral_B_toothpicks_dental_woodsticks.jpg/500px-Oral_B_toothpicks_dental_woodsticks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Oral B toothpicks","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOral_B_toothpicks_dental_woodsticks.jpg"},{"srcset":"https:/